From 5a364d99f656f56747f5aa9302e3f60260383e49 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Tue, 24 Feb 2026 17:50:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Unihertz 8849 hardware controls

Add a settings menu for the Unihertz 8849 (Tank) device-specific
hardware, detected via the Agold HAL and FPGA sysfs interface.

Features:
- Warning light with red/blue/green modes (ioctl 310)
- Camping light with off/full/medium/low/flash/SOS modes (ioctl 301)
- Projector enable/disable matching stock powerOnOffForPrejectorOn/Off
  sequence: display resize, AoD disable, sleep/wake via PowerManager,
  ioctl 500 sub-commands (0,4 / 0,6 / mode / 0,3), calibration
- Projector mode selection (portrait, landscape, landscape inverted)
- Phone display toggle while projecting
- Projector brightness, manual keystone, fan speed
- Auto-keystone correction via accelerometer (exact replica of stock
  ProjectorController.calculateOrientation: 10-sample accumulation,
  3-second cycle, 1.68*0.4 scaling, GSI sign correction)
- Per-device factory focus calibration read from proinfo partition
  (offset 0x1000cc for focus table, 0x10014c for AWB/H3 scan)
- Focus calibration sweep via motor_turn_mode_step with dmesg parsing
- Manual focus adjustment via motor_turn_mode_step
- Projector temperature and laser rangefinder readout
- Display viewport shrinks to 16:9 when projector is active

The projector enable sequence sends ioctl 500 0 0 4 (disable display),
sleeps via PowerManager.goToSleep(), waits for projector_sys_status==0,
sends ioctl 500 0 0 6 (hardware init, ignored if unsupported), wakes
via PowerManager.wakeUp(), sets projector mode, then re-enables phone
display with ioctl 500 0 0 3. AoD is temporarily disabled during
sleep/wake to prevent the display staying in Doze state.

Focus calibration is loaded from the proinfo factory partition on first
boot and stored in SharedPreferences. The default hardcoded values are
only used as a fallback if proinfo read fails.
